    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nTraditional seafront farmstead, enjoying a sunny, west facing aspect, located within the scenic Rossbrin Cove between Schull and Ballydehob in West Cork. Rossbrin Cove is the ideal sailing location to access the myriad of islands that form part of the famed Carberys Hundred Isles. Planning Permission is granted for the restoration of this unique opportunity, set on 1.1 acres and offering a rare opportunity to create a beautiful coastal home with already restored studio and a workshop in a most spectacular seafront setting.\n\nOccupying a wonderful tranquil waterfront position with mooring, the property enjoys a sunny position with breathtaking views across the water towards Rossbrin Castle. The vibrant coastal villages and islands are easily accessed from Rosssbrin Cove.\n\nAt the heart of the property is a charming traditional stone-built farmhouse, retaining much of the character and appeal of its original construction. Full planning permission has been granted for the restoration and extension of the existing farmhouse property, providing an exciting opportunity to transform this historic coastal dwelling into a superb modern home while retaining its distinctive character.\n\nThe plans provide for a thoughtfully designed residence incorporating generous living accommodation, bedrooms and modern amenities with the layout carefully considered to take full advantage of the property's exceptional position and views. Also included is a completed detached garage/studio/ workshop, offering further flexibility for the future owner and currently in use as temporary accommodation.\n\nA particularly special feature of the property is the private mooring, providing direct access to the water and the extraordinary network of islands, coves and waterways that make Roaringwater Bay such a sought-after destination for boating and water-based activities. For those who enjoy sailing, kayaking, fishing, swimming or simply being close to the sea, this is a truly enviable location.\n\nThe property is conveniently positioned close to both Schull and Ballydehob, two vibrant and much-loved West Cork villages offering a selection of cafés, restaurants, pubs, shops, schools and everyday amenities. The surrounding area is renowned for its beautiful coastline, sailing waters, beaches and islands while the larger towns of Skibbereen and Bantry are within easy reach.\n\nDisclaimer:\nWhilst every care has been taken in the preparation of these particulars, all information is provided in good faith and is believed to be correct, but is not guaranteed. Interested parties should satisfy themselves as to the accuracy and completeness of all details by independent inspection or enquiry. No representation or warranty is made regarding the condition, measurements, boundaries, planning status, services or other information relating to the property. All measurements, maps, photographs and distances are approximate and for guidance purposes only. Photographs, video and drone imagery are provided for illustrative purposes and may include features, furnishings or items not included in the sale."
      },
